  "output": "\n\nOn it — building a birthday-card generator mini-app with a contact picker, message drafting, and a rendered card. Let me pull the design doc, the contacts store, and the owner-data rules first.\n\nThe scratch write was blocked earlier, so let me extract the design doc's component list straight from the saved output.\n\nThe design doc is one giant line, so I'll extract just the fragments I need around the API signatures.\n\nAPI surface is clear. Scaffolding the app now, then I'll write the source.\n\nA birthday-cards workspace already exists from Sep 23 — let me see what's in it before rebuilding.\n\nThis workspace is the same request from earlier this week — plan and source already written. Let me check where the last build left off.\n\nThe workspace is from the same request on Sep 25 — code is complete and a build already succeeded with zero findings. Let me check where it stalled (looks like QA/dev release never ran).\n\nSame story across six builds since Sep 22: build always succeeded, QA and dev release never ran. I'll pick up exactly there — QA now.\n\nQA on this control plane runs through the V13 job lane — `air-create go` is the path that drives build, QA, tests, and the dev release. Starting it.\n\nThe build pipeline is the only lane this control plane runs — QA, tests, and the dev channel are all switched off (\"preview unavailable\", \"dev channel unavailable\", \"v13_disabled\"), which is where this stalled on the 25th. The good news: the generator itself is done and the build is clean.\n\nBuilt and staged as a draft (0 findings, 0 hard): pick a person from your list — seeded with Marcus Lee from your contacts, plus an add-row for anyone else with an optional birthday — draft the message from warm/funny/short templates, then it renders an 800×1000 card on canvas with a Save-image button. One honest caveat: your contacts store has no birthdays in it, so the app keeps its own list rather than syncing, and QA couldn't run here since there's 